        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "16432f7c-d943-3f4d-9326-03fc49ae7746",
                "word": "hypertexte",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2cac27d1-3d26-4ef4-8c42-3f6b57d46a09",
                        "entry_id": "16432f7c-d943-3f4d-9326-03fc49ae7746",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hypertextes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7b06997a-38c5-380a-842c-5fae7d7435e2",
                        "entry_id": "16432f7c-d943-3f4d-9326-03fc49ae7746",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Système de renvois, via des hyperliens permettant de passer directement d’une partie d’un document à une autre, ou d’un document à d’autres documents choisis comme pertinents par l’auteur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Internet"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "362ea351-b376-4802-a02a-f04b47f98b59",
                                "sense_id": "7b06997a-38c5-380a-842c-5fae7d7435e2",
                                "text": "[…] Il t’expliquerait alors qu’un hypertexte est un texte augmenté de liens qui vont au-delà de ce texte en invitant le lecteur à consulter d’autres textes et, surtout, à en faciliter l’accès, autrement dit que c’est un texte plus puissant qu’un texte, à savoir un hypertexte..."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e2b6a5a-8e4c-3b95-aa2d-8fe522b18e2a",
                        "entry_id": "16432f7c-d943-3f4d-9326-03fc49ae7746",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dans la terminologie de Gérard Genette, tout texte B uni à un texte antérieur A par une relation d’hypertextualité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Critique littéraire"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "56dfa364-7c2b-4093-9fd8-626574463236",
                        "source_entry_id": "16432f7c-d943-3f4d-9326-03fc49ae7746",
                        "target_lang_word": "Hypertext",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Hypertext",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49576110-789c-34d8-8f9f-b5a9a296ee32",
                                        "entry_id": "ba6572f2-f4f2-306b-b13f-7ac846efb43b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Menge von Schriften (Texten), die durch Querverweise oder Hyperlinks (auch Links genannt) miteinander verbunden sind"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f2be182-90ca-418a-aebe-252bbb78e5f9",
                                                "sense_id": "49576110-789c-34d8-8f9f-b5a9a296ee32",
                                                "text": "„Ein typischer Hypertext besteht aus sogenannten Kanten und Knoten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82727547-e73d-4600-9b93-363be60710fe",
                                                "sense_id": "49576110-789c-34d8-8f9f-b5a9a296ee32",
                                                "text": "„Hypertexte hingegen sind netzartige Texte, in denen die Konventionen des zweidimensionalen Textes mehr oder weniger (das entscheiden die Autoren) durch andere, neue Konventionen ersetzt werden.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6058a846-5047-4a9a-9972-089d82ef61fa",
                                                "sense_id": "49576110-789c-34d8-8f9f-b5a9a296ee32",
                                                "text": "„Es gibt zwar neue Textsorten: elektronische Textsorten wie Hypertexte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "44d0e803-67ff-4ec9-94a6-eff49f58d512",
                        "source_entry_id": "16432f7c-d943-3f4d-9326-03fc49ae7746",
                        "target_lang_word": "hypertext",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hypertext",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53654231-7890-3ab4-b94a-7de98ebd23bd",
                                        "entry_id": "a8c895f8-76ad-3d82-8a26-fb34192a833e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Digital text in which the reader may navigate related information through embedded hyperlinks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b6e59c2-4f93-422b-9c2a-3ba2cb025143",
                                                "sense_id": "53654231-7890-3ab4-b94a-7de98ebd23bd",
                                                "text": "We do not read hypertext the same way we read a novel, and browsing the Web is a different experience from reading a book or newspaper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ffeb614-3c13-48c8-8d0e-4c791bf6875f",
                                                "sense_id": "53654231-7890-3ab4-b94a-7de98ebd23bd",
                                                "text": "Further, hypertext systems, because of their ease of construction, are very rich in text, graphics and visual illustrations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "432ff180-eebc-4d6f-a45b-1769efdfe8de",
                                                "sense_id": "53654231-7890-3ab4-b94a-7de98ebd23bd",
                                                "text": "1995, Gary Wolf, \"The Curse of Xanadu\", WIRED\nDid Nelson realize at the time that he had met Xanadu's second parent? Probably not. The inventor scattered his ideas as widely as possible, with little care about where they landed. But as the decades passed, it would be Gregory who oversaw the attempt to transform Xanadu into a real product. He never received much public notice, but through all the project's painful deaths and rebirths, Gregory's commitment to Nelson's dream of a universal hypertext library never waned. If Ted Nelson is Xanadu's profligate father, Roger Gregory is Xanadu's devoted mother, and in retrospect, his role appears to have been intertwined with a terrible element of sacrifice."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ae6d842-7466-3118-af74-c7839e7c3708",
                                        "entry_id": "a8c895f8-76ad-3d82-8a26-fb34192a833e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hypertext document."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3746700-c386-4a79-a560-5799213d786c",
                                                "sense_id": "1ae6d842-7466-3118-af74-c7839e7c3708",
                                                "text": "A hypertext system, then, is a memex-like device for creating and manipulating hypertexts, both for on-line browsing, and for reducing selected portions of such texts to . ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "23aae762-8c4f-49c6-88df-cd633f476564",
                        "source_entry_id": "16432f7c-d943-3f4d-9326-03fc49ae7746",
